# xcquinox.alec.cluster — rsync filter rules for the "summaries" pull profile.
#
# Loaded via `rsync --filter='. <abs path>/summaries.filter'`. Rules apply with
# the run dir (`run_<UTC>Z/`) as the transfer root, so leading `/` anchors a
# pattern to that root (NOT the filesystem root). See `man rsync` "FILTER RULES"
# and "INCLUDE/EXCLUDE PATTERN RULES".
#
# Contract: this filter MUST stay in sync with the artifact layout the harness
# writes (see xcquinox/alec/cluster/__main__.py cmd_submit, _train_task.py,
# _eval_one_spec.py, _pretrain.py). When the harness gains a new small artifact,
# add a `+ ` line here in the same commit. The end-to-end canary test in
# tests/test_cluster_sync.py drives rsync against a fixture tree and will fail
# loudly if this filter omits an artifact it lists or includes a *.eqx blob it
# is not supposed to.

# --- top-level metadata (small, always wanted) -----------------------------
+ /manifest.json
+ /resolved_config.yaml
+ /jobs.json
+ /attempts.json

# --- per-spec eval / training summaries ------------------------------------
# rsync needs `+ <dir>/` rules to descend into each level; the final `- *`
# below would otherwise prune the whole subtree.
+ /checkpoints/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_df.csv
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/failure.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/losses.npy
# aux_log.pkl (per-step, per-group, per-channel loss values) + train_metadata
# (config + final_loss) are the FIRST things needed to triage a NaN/divergent
# run -- small (~90 KB/spec), so pull them in `summaries` rather than forcing a
# multi-GB `--profile full`. (2026-06: a polarized-correlation NaN was diagnosed
# from aux_log.pkl, which the summaries profile had been dropping.)
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/aux_log.pkl
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/train_metadata.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval/per_molecule.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval/skipped.json
# Held-out (BH76 + W4-11) reaction-energy eval -- THE "beats PBE?" headline:
# eval_holdout/test_set.csv (mae_nn vs mae_pbe vs delta), per_reaction.json,
# per_molecule.json, and failure.json. This dir holds ONLY small text
# (CSV/JSON, no *.eqx), so `***` pulls the whole subtree present + future.
# (2026-06: the summaries profile had been dropping eval_holdout/ entirely, so
# the headline metric never reached a default pull -- guarded by the canary.)
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout/***
# Best-loss-checkpoint held-out eval (2026-06): a SECOND eval pass over the same
# pool using model_best.eqx instead of the final-step model.eqx, written to a
# sibling eval_holdout_best/ (same small CSV/JSON artifacts, no *.eqx). Doubles
# the figure data return; pulled by default like its eval_holdout/ sibling.
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_best/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_best/***
# Validation-best-checkpoint held-out eval (2026-06): a THIRD eval pass over the
# same pool using model_val_best.eqx (the held-out-VALIDATION-best weights). This
# is the checkpoint the figures now plot as "val-best" -- unlike model_best.eqx
# (min TRAINING loss, which selects the most-overfit step) it does not collapse on
# overfit-prone archs. Same small CSV/JSON, no *.eqx; pulled by default like its
# eval_holdout/ siblings so the default figures-only pull has the data.
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_val_best/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_val_best/***

# --- pretrain metadata + loss curves (small, useful for diagnostics) -------
+ /pretrain/
+ /pretrain/*/
+ /pretrain/*/pretrain_metadata.json
+ /pretrain/*/losses_*.npy

# --- drop everything else -------------------------------------------------
# This includes: /logs/, /scripts/, /specs/, every *.eqx model checkpoint,
# every per-spec *.gen<N> archived artifact, and any future top-level dir
# the harness gains (must be opted in explicitly above).
- *
